#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""Stand-in for the `agy` CLI (Antigravity CLI 1.5.17).

It looks and reports like the real CLI towards the app and towards a person
looking at the terminal, and never calls a model or the network. Observed
behaviour of the real CLI: the "agy" section of
docs/clawddy-refactor/cli-facts.md (probes of 2026-11-25 against 1.5.17).
The input decoding, the event loop, the drawing machinery and the script
director are the `claude` stand-in's, loaded from the file beside this one;
what agy does differently is here.

What it does
- Arguments: --prompt-interactive=TEXT (also -i TEXT), --conversation ID
  (also -r, --resume), --add-dir DIR (repeatable), --dangerously-skip-
  permissions, --model ID, --effort LEVEL, --mode accept-edits|auto|plan,
  --settings JSON-or-file (only "agentMode" is read; "" is default mode).
  Other flags are accepted and ignored; --print is refused. `--version`
  prints the version as the real one does.
- Its data folder stands for ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli and is
  $AGY_STANDIN_DATA_DIR, or <dir>/agy-data where <dir>/bin holds this
  program. It never reads or writes the person's home. In it:
  conversations/<id>.db (empty; the conversation exists),
  presence/<id>.lock (held with flock while this process has the
  conversation open; the file stays after exit, as the real one's does),
  brain/<id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl (the transcript, in
  the real format: one JSON object per step, USER_INPUT, PLANNER_RESPONSE,
  GENERIC).
- A conversation exists only after the first prompt: its id is made then,
  its lock taken, SessionStart runs. --conversation with an id that exists
  (a conversation file, or a script under that id) resumes it: the lock is
  taken at start and SessionStart never runs, not even at the first prompt.
  An id that does not exist is ignored without a word, as the real one does:
  the first prompt makes a new id. /clear (or /new) moves to a new id at once
  (lock included); its SessionStart runs at the next prompt. Not modelled: the
  real one remembers the folders a conversation was made with and adds them
  back on a resume.
- Terminal: raw mode, bracketed paste, kitty keyboard flags pushed
  (ESC[>5u), as the real one. A banner, the transcript, then the bottom area:
  spinner and queued messages while working, the input box between two
  full-width rules ("> " and the text; empty it shows the mode's hint until
  anything was typed in this process, then a bare ">"; a hint longer than
  the terminal's width less 3 is cut to it and ends "...", as captured at 44
  and 60 columns), and the footer (left:
  "? for shortcuts", "esc to cancel", "  Press up to edit queued messages",
  "press ctrl+c again to exit", or nothing while text is typed; right:
  "<mode> · <model> · <effort>", no mode in default mode). Each submitted
  prompt is echoed above as a 60-cell rule and "> text".
- Status reports (OSC 7501, BEL-terminated, app=antigravity, fields in the
  order state, kind, app, msg): it asks `7501;?` at start and reports only
  once the terminal answers. Then `blocked kind=auth` "Sign in required",
  and `idle` 0.03 s later (0.5 s when resuming: the longest seen, on two
  resumes; others took 0.03 s), or `blocked kind=permission`
  "Trust this folder?" when the script asks for the trust dialog. A turn:
  `working` at once (with the conversation's title as msg when resumed and
  the script names one), `done` with the reply's first line as msg (cut to
  199 characters and "…" past 200), sent after the Stop hook returns. A
  question: `blocked kind=question` with the question as msg (cut to 179 and
  "…" past 180). A permission menu: `blocked kind=permission` "Approve Bash:
  <command>". A failure: `error` with the error text; no hook runs. The first
  key after `done` or `error` reports `idle`. Exit reports `idle`.
- Hooks: .agents/hooks.json of the working folder and of each added folder
  is read at start ({"name": {"enabled": bool, "<Event>": [{"type":
  "command", "command": "...", "timeout": 30}, ...]}}; matcher groups with a
  "hooks" list are read too). SessionStart, PreInvocation, PostInvocation and
  Stop run through `/bin/sh -c` with that .agents folder as the working
  folder, ANTIGRAVITY_CONVERSATION_ID set, and the record on stdin: sorted
  keys, camelCase, as the real ones (artifactDirectoryPath, conversationId,
  cwd, hookEventName, lastUserInput, modelName, transcriptPath,
  workspacePaths; PreInvocation/PostInvocation add initialNumSteps and
  invocationNum; Stop adds continuationActive, error, executionNum,
  fullyIdle, terminationReason "NO_TOOL_CALL"). Paths under $HOME are
  written with "~" as the real ones are. What a hook prints is ignored. A
  hook that fails or times out adds a line "⚠ <Event> hook failed ..." (the
  stand-in's own wording; nothing about this is captured). The transcript
  holds the turn's reply before Stop runs. An interrupted turn runs no
  further hook and writes nothing more to the transcript.
- Keys: typing edits the box; paste inserts as typed; Return submits. While
  working a submitted message is queued ("▸ text (alt+m to send
  immediately)") and sent as the next turn when the turn ends; several are
  sent together as one prompt, joined by newlines, in one turn (captured,
  probes/stage5/queue2: PreInvocation 0 with "one.\ntwo.", one Stop). Escape (or
  Control-C) while working interrupts: `idle`, "⎿  Interrupted · What should
  Antigravity CLI do instead?", queued text goes back into the box. Escape on
  a question or permission menu interrupts too (not captured). With text in
  an idle box, Escape twice within 0.3 s empties it. Control-C with no turn
  arms "press ctrl+c again to exit" (the text stays); the second Control-C
  exits. Control-D on an empty box arms "press ctrl+d again to exit"; the
  second exits; with text it does nothing. Shift+Tab cycles default,
  accept-edits, auto, plan. On exit it prints "Resume with -c (or command
  below):" and "agy --conversation=<id>" when a conversation exists.
  SIGTERM and SIGHUP end it the same way.

Key log: as the `claude` stand-in, under the conversation id.

The script file: <dir>/standin/<conversation id>.json, else
<dir>/standin/default.json, in the `claude` stand-in's format (its "screen"
LINEs and "steps"), with these differences:
  "title":  the conversation's title: the msg of `working` when resumed
  "trust":  true shows agy's folder-trust dialog first ("Yes" selected);
            a first prompt's turn runs behind it with its hooks and no
            report; "No, exit" leaves as the real one does (idle, status 0)
  steps:    {"permission": "make test"}   a Bash call that needs approval
                                          (runs at once with --dangerously-
                                          skip-permissions)
            {"wake": "Waiting.", "after": 2}
                                          a background command: that reply
                                          and Stop, then after 2 s agy's own
                                          PreInvocation 0 with the turn's
                                          prompt; the next steps follow
            {"fail": KIND, "text": "..."} every kind reports `error`
            {"finish": "text"}            "summary", "plus", "minus" unused
  A prompt submitted while no turn is open opens one; its work is the next
  steps, or the default turn (a few tool lines and a short reply).
"""
import base64
import collections
import datetime
import fcntl
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import termios
import textwrap
import time
import tty
import uuid

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True  # no cache files beside the stand-ins
_loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(
    "claude_standin", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(sys.argv[0])), "claude"))
base = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader(_loader.name, _loader))
_loader.exec_module(base)

VERSION = "1.5.17"
rgb = base.rgb
RESET, BOLD, INV = base.RESET, base.BOLD, base.INV
BLUE, GREY, RULE = rgb(138, 180, 248), rgb(154, 160, 166), rgb(60, 64, 67)
AMBER, LIGHT, TEXT, RED = rgb(249, 171, 0), rgb(189, 193, 198), rgb(232, 234, 237), rgb(242, 139, 130)
SPIN = "⣾⣽⣻⢿⡿⣟⣯⣷"
MODES = ["", "accept-edits", "auto", "plan"]  # the order Shift+Tab cycles
HINTS = {"accept-edits": "Accept-edits mode: file edits auto-approved (shift+tab to cycle)",
         "auto": "Auto mode: edits & safe commands auto-approved (shift+tab to cycle)",
         "plan": "Plan mode: research & plan only (shift+tab to cycle)"}
INTERRUPTED = "Interrupted · What should Antigravity CLI do instead?"
PERMISSION_OPTIONS = ["Yes, run command",
                      "Yes, and always allow in this conversation for commands that start with '{w}'",
                      "Yes, and always allow for commands that start with '{w}' (Persist to settings.json)",
                      "No, cancel"]
TRUST_OPTIONS = ["Yes, I trust this folder", "No, exit"]
TRUST_MSG = "Trust this folder?"
FAILED = "failed to construct executor: plan model not specified; you must specify a valid model"
VALUES = {"--conversation": "conversation", "-r": "conversation", "--resume": "conversation",
          "--prompt-interactive": "prompt", "-i": "prompt", "--add-dir": "add_dir", "--model": "model",
          "--effort": "effort", "--mode": "mode", "--settings": "settings", "--agent": None, "--project": None,
          "--log-file": None, "--print-timeout": None, "--input-format": None, "--output-format": None,
          "--json-schema": None}


def parse_args(argv):
    o = {"conversation": None, "prompt": None, "add_dir": [], "model": None, "effort": None, "mode": None,
         "settings": None, "skip": False}
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        flag, eq, v = argv[i].partition("=")
        i += 1
        if flag in ("-p", "--print", "--prompt"):
            sys.exit("agy: the stand-in has no print mode")
        if flag in VALUES:
            if not eq:
                if i >= len(argv):
                    sys.exit(f"agy: {flag} needs a value")
                v = argv[i]
                i += 1
            key = VALUES[flag]
            if key == "add_dir":
                o["add_dir"].append(v)
            elif key:
                o[key] = v
        elif flag == "--dangerously-skip-permissions":
            o["skip"] = True
        # Any other flag or word is accepted and ignored.
    return o


def cut(text, limit):
    return text if len(text) <= limit else text[:limit - 1] + "…"


def b64(text):
    return base64.b64encode(text.encode()).decode()


def wrap(text, width):
    """Text as rows of at most `width` characters, broken between words, as agy wraps."""
    return [row for line in text.split("\n") for row in textwrap.wrap(line, max(1, width)) or [""]]


def now_utc():
    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


class Agy(base.StandIn):
    def __init__(self, o):
        self.o = o
        self.cwd = os.getcwd()
        self.data = os.environ.get("AGY_STANDIN_DATA_DIR") or os.path.join(base.HARNESS, "agy-data")
        self.workspaces = [self.cwd] + [os.path.abspath(d) for d in o["add_dir"]]
        settings = {}
        if o["settings"]:
            s = o["settings"]
            settings = json.loads(s) if s.lstrip().startswith("{") else json.load(open(s))
        mode = o["mode"] if o["mode"] is not None else settings.get("agentMode", "auto")
        self.agent_mode = "" if mode == "default" else mode
        if self.agent_mode not in MODES:
            sys.exit(f"agy: unknown mode {mode!r}")
        self.model = o["model"] or "example-model"
        self.effort = o["effort"] or "high"
        asked = o["conversation"]
        self.resumed = bool(asked) and self.conversation_exists(asked)
        self.sid = asked if self.resumed else None
        self.script = base.load_script([asked] if self.resumed else [])
        sc = self.script
        self.title_text = sc.get("title")
        self.folder = sc.get("folder") or self.cwd
        self.first_prompt = o["prompt"]
        self.hooks = self.load_hooks()
        self.lock_fd = None
        self.new_conversation = False  # SessionStart is due at the next prompt
        self.step_index = self.transcript_lines() if self.sid else 0
        self.last_input = ""
        self.status_ok = False
        self.reported = None
        self.signed_in = False
        # transcript and screen
        self.entries = [("header", "")]
        for line in sc.get("screen", []):
            self.add(base.entry_of(line))
            if line.startswith("> "):
                self.last_input = line[2:]
        self.printed = 0
        self.dyn_rows = 0
        self.dirty = True
        self.full = True
        # input
        self.inbuf = b""
        self.esc_at = None
        self.pasting = False
        self.paste = b""
        self.input, self.cur = "", 0
        self.typed = False  # anything typed in this process hides the mode's hint for good
        self.esc_idle_at = None
        self.armed = None  # "ctrl-c" or "ctrl-d": the next press exits
        self.dialog = {"sel": 0} if sc.get("trust") else None
        # turns
        self.turn_open = False
        self.turn_prompt = None
        self.turn_started = 0.0
        self.invocation = 0
        self.queue = []
        self.asking = None
        self.permission = None
        self.last_answer = None
        self.unclaimed = None
        # script
        self.steps = collections.deque(sc.get("steps", []))
        self.gen = None
        self.begun = False
        self.waiting = None
        self.timers = []
        self.signal = None
        self.winch = False
        self.hung = False

    # ---- the data folder ----
    def conversation_exists(self, cid):
        return base.safe_name(cid) and (
            os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.data, "conversations", cid + ".db"))
            or os.path.exists(os.path.join(base.HARNESS, "standin", cid + ".json")))

    def tilde(self, path):
        home = os.environ.get("HOME", "")
        return "~" + path[len(home):] if home and path.startswith(home.rstrip("/") + "/") else path

    def brain(self):
        return os.path.join(self.data, "brain", self.sid)

    def transcript_path(self):
        return os.path.join(self.brain(), ".system_generated", "logs", "transcript_full.jsonl")

    def transcript_lines(self):
        path = self.transcript_path()
        return sum(1 for _ in open(path)) if os.path.exists(path) else 0

    def log_step(self, kind, **fields):
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.transcript_path()), exist_ok=True)
        line = {"step_index": self.step_index, "source": "USER_EXPLICIT" if kind == "USER_INPUT" else "MODEL",
                "type": kind, "status": "DONE", "created_at": now_utc(), **fields}
        with open(self.transcript_path(), "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(line) + "\n")
        self.step_index += 1

    def model_step(self, **fields):
        self.log_step("PLANNER_RESPONSE", model=self.model, input_tokens=2400, cache_read_tokens=8500,
                      output_tokens=32, **fields)

    def take_lock(self):
        """Holds presence/<id>.lock. A second process on the same id is not refused, as with the real one."""
        if self.lock_fd is not None:
            os.close(self.lock_fd)
        folder = os.path.join(self.data, "presence")
        os.makedirs(folder, exist_ok=True)
        fd = os.open(os.path.join(folder, self.sid + ".lock"), os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            os.close(fd)
            fd = None
        self.lock_fd = fd

    def new_id(self):
        self.sid = str(uuid.uuid4())
        self.step_index = 0
        self.new_conversation = True
        self.resumed = False
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(self.data, "conversations"), exist_ok=True)
        open(os.path.join(self.data, "conversations", self.sid + ".db"), "a").close()
        self.take_lock()

    # ---- hooks ----
    def load_hooks(self):
        found = []
        for folder in self.workspaces:
            path = os.path.join(folder, ".agents", "hooks.json")
            if not os.path.exists(path):
                continue
            with open(path) as f:
                named = json.load(f)
            for definition in named.values():
                if definition.get("enabled", True) is False:
                    continue
                for event in ("SessionStart", "PreInvocation", "PostInvocation", "Stop"):
                    for item in definition.get(event, []):
                        for h in item["hooks"] if "hooks" in item else [item]:
                            if h.get("type", "command") == "command":
                                found.append((event, os.path.dirname(path), h["command"], h.get("timeout", 30)))
        return found

    def hook(self, event, **fields):
        if self.sid is None:
            return
        record = {"artifactDirectoryPath": self.tilde(self.brain()), "conversationId": self.sid, "cwd": self.cwd,
                  "hookEventName": event, "lastUserInput": self.last_input, "modelName": self.model,
                  "transcriptPath": self.tilde(self.transcript_path()), "workspacePaths": self.workspaces, **fields}
        data = json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True)
        env = dict(os.environ, ANTIGRAVITY_CONVERSATION_ID=self.sid)
        for ev, folder, command, timeout in self.hooks:
            if ev != event:
                continue
            try:
                r = subprocess.run(["/bin/sh", "-c", command], input=data, text=True, capture_output=True,
                                   timeout=timeout, cwd=folder, env=env)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                self.add(("err", f"{event} hook failed: timed out after {timeout}s"))
                continue
            if r.returncode != 0:
                self.add(("err", f"{event} hook failed with status {r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()[:200]}"))

    def invocation_hook(self, event):
        self.hook(event, initialNumSteps=self.step_index, invocationNum=self.invocation)

    # ---- output ----
    def report(self, state, kind=None, msg=None):
        self.reported = (state, kind, msg)
        # A turn run behind the trust dialog reports nothing (captured,
        # probes/stage5/trustprompt: hooks only, no working or done).
        if not self.status_ok or (self.dialog and state != "blocked"):
            return
        body = f"7501;state={state}" + (f":kind={kind}" if kind else "") + ":app=antigravity"
        if msg:
            body += ":msg=" + b64(msg)
        self.write("\x1b]" + body + "\x07")

    def to_idle(self):
        """The first key after a finished or failed turn reports idle."""
        if self.reported and self.reported[0] in ("done", "error") and not self.turn_open:
            self.report("idle")

    # ---- turns ----
    def start_turn(self, prompt):
        self.turn_open = True
        self.turn_prompt = prompt
        self.turn_started = time.monotonic()
        self.invocation = 0
        self.armed = None
        self.dirty = True
        if prompt is not None:
            self.add(("you", prompt))
        self.report("working", msg=self.title_text if self.resumed else None)
        if prompt is not None:
            if self.sid is None:
                self.new_id()
            self.last_input = prompt
            local = datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
            self.log_step("USER_INPUT", content=f"<USER_REQUEST>\n{prompt}\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\n"
                                                f"The current local time is: {local}.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>")
            if self.new_conversation:
                self.new_conversation = False
                self.hook("SessionStart")
            self.invocation_hook("PreInvocation")
        self.unclaimed = prompt
        if self.waiting and self.waiting[0] in ("wait", "prompt"):
            self.unclaimed = None
            self.run_director(prompt)

    def end_turn(self):
        self.turn_open = False
        self.asking = None
        self.permission = None
        self.dirty = True
        if self.queue:
            # A queued message is sent as the next turn.
            queued, self.queue = "\n".join(self.queue), []
            self.later(0.05, lambda: self.submit(queued))

    def tool_done(self, result):
        """A tool step finished: its result, then the model is called again."""
        if self.sid:
            self.log_step("GENERIC", content=f"Created At: {now_utc()}\nCompleted At: {now_utc()}\n{result}")
        self.invocation_hook("PostInvocation")
        self.invocation += 1
        self.invocation_hook("PreInvocation")

    def add_line(self, line):
        e = base.entry_of(line)
        self.add(e)
        if not self.turn_open:
            return
        if e[0] == "tool" and self.sid:
            m = re.match(r"([A-Za-z]+)\((.*)\)$", e[1])
            name, args = (m.group(1), m.group(2)) if m else (e[1], "")
            self.model_step(tool_calls=[{"name": "run_command" if name == "Bash" else name, "args": {"input": args}}])
        elif e[0] == "out":
            self.tool_done(e[1])

    def finish(self, message, summary=None, plus=0, minus=0):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        self.add(("text", message))
        if self.sid:
            self.model_step(content=message)
        self.invocation_hook("PostInvocation")
        self.hook("Stop", continuationActive=False, error="", executionNum=0, fullyIdle=True,
                  terminationReason="NO_TOOL_CALL")
        self.draw()
        self.report("done", msg=cut(message.split("\n")[0], 200))
        self.end_turn()

    def wake(self, waiting, after):
        """A command left running in the background (captured,
        probes/stage5/wake2): the turn's reply so far and its Stop, still
        `working`; after `after` seconds agy starts invocation 0 itself,
        `lastUserInput` the turn's prompt, the transcript's last step the
        reply. The script's next steps are that invocation's."""
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        self.add(("text", waiting))
        if self.sid:
            self.model_step(content=waiting)
        self.invocation_hook("PostInvocation")
        self.hook("Stop", continuationActive=False, error="", executionNum=0, fullyIdle=True,
                  terminationReason="NO_TOOL_CALL")
        self.draw()
        yield ("wait", after)
        self.invocation = 0
        self.invocation_hook("PreInvocation")

    def fail(self, kind, text=None, resets=None):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        text = text or FAILED
        self.add(("err", text))
        self.add(("plain", f"{GREY}Error ID: {uuid.uuid4()}-1{RESET}"))
        self.draw()
        self.report("error", msg=text)
        self.end_turn()

    def ask(self, question, options, header):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        if self.sid:
            self.model_step(tool_calls=[{"name": "ask_question", "args": {"questions": [
                {"is_multi_select": False, "options": options, "question": question}]}}])
        self.add(("ask", question))
        self.asking = {"q": question, "options": options, "sel": 0}
        self.draw()
        self.report("blocked", kind="question", msg=cut(question, 180))

    def answer(self, text):
        self.asking = None
        self.input, self.cur = "", 0
        self.add(("answer", text))
        self.last_answer = text
        self.report("working", msg=self.title_text if self.resumed else None)
        self.tool_done(f"A1: {text}")
        if self.waiting and self.waiting[0] == "answer":
            self.run_director(text)

    def ask_permission(self, command):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        if self.sid:
            self.model_step(tool_calls=[{"name": "run_command", "args": {"CommandLine": command}}])
        self.add(("tool", f"Bash({command})"))
        if self.o["skip"]:
            self.tool_done("")
            return False
        self.permission = {"command": command, "sel": 0}
        self.draw()
        self.report("blocked", kind="permission", msg=f"Approve Bash: {command}")
        return True

    def permit(self, sel):
        self.permission = None
        if sel == len(PERMISSION_OPTIONS) - 1:
            self.add(("out", "Cancelled"))  # the stand-in's own wording; not captured
        self.report("working", msg=self.title_text if self.resumed else None)
        self.tool_done("" if sel < 3 else "cancelled")
        if self.waiting and self.waiting[0] == "permission":
            self.run_director()

    def interrupt(self):
        if not self.turn_open:
            return
        queued, self.queue = self.queue, []
        if queued:
            self.input = "\n".join(queued + ([self.input] if self.input else []))
            self.cur = len(self.input)
        self.add(("interrupted", INTERRUPTED))
        self.turn_open = False
        self.asking = None
        self.permission = None
        self.report("idle")
        if self.gen:
            self.gen.close()
        while self.steps:
            st = self.steps.popleft()
            if "finish" in st or "fail" in st:
                break
        self.unclaimed = None
        self.gen = self.director()
        self.run_director()

    def clear_conversation(self):
        """/clear: a new conversation id at once; its SessionStart comes with the next prompt."""
        self.entries = [("header", "")]
        self.full = True
        self.new_id()

    # ---- the script ----
    def do_step(self, st):
        if "print" in st:
            rate = st.get("rate", 5)
            for line in st["print"]:
                self.add_line(line)
                yield ("sleep", 1.0 / rate)
        elif "working" in st:
            if not self.turn_open:
                self.start_turn(None)
            self.turn_started = time.monotonic() - st.get("elapsed", 0)
            self.dirty = True
        elif "finish" in st:
            self.finish(st["finish"])
        elif "ask" in st:
            self.ask(st["ask"], st.get("options", []), st.get("header"))
            yield ("answer",)
        elif "permission" in st:
            if self.ask_permission(st["permission"]):
                yield ("permission",)
        elif "fail" in st:
            self.fail(st["fail"], st.get("text"))
        elif "wake" in st:
            yield from self.wake(st["wake"], float(st.get("after", 2)))
        elif "wait" in st:
            yield ("prompt",) if st["wait"] == "prompt" else ("wait", float(st["wait"]))
        else:
            raise ValueError(f"unknown step in the stand-in script: {st}")

    def default_work(self, prompt):
        words = re.findall(r"[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}", prompt or "")
        w = max(words, key=len).lower() if words else "task"
        yield ("sleep", 0.5)
        for call, result in ((f"⏺ Bash(rg -n {w} src)", f"⎿ src/{w}.py:12: def {w}():"),
                             ("⏺ Bash(make test)", "⎿ 48 passed")):
            self.add_line(call)
            yield ("sleep", 0.4)
            self.add_line(result)
            yield ("sleep", 0.4)
        said = " ".join((self.turn_prompt or prompt or "the task").split())
        said = said if len(said) <= 70 else said[:69] + "…"
        self.finish(f"Done: {said}.\nOne file changed and the 48 tests pass.")

    # ---- input ----
    def submit(self, text):
        if text.strip() in ("/clear", "/new") and not self.turn_open:
            return self.clear_conversation()
        if self.turn_open:
            self.queue.append(text)
            self.dirty = True
            return
        self.start_turn(text)

    def insert(self, text):
        self.to_idle()
        self.typed = True
        super().insert(text)

    def key(self, k):
        self.keylog(k)
        self.dirty = True
        self.to_idle()
        if self.dialog:
            return self.dialog_key(k)
        if k != "esc":
            self.esc_idle_at = None
        a, p = self.asking, self.permission
        menu = a or p
        if k == "enter":
            if a:
                if a["sel"] < len(a["options"]):
                    return self.answer(a["options"][a["sel"]])
                return self.answer(self.input.strip()) if self.input.strip() else None
            if p:
                return self.permit(p["sel"])
            text, self.input, self.cur = self.input, "", 0
            if text.strip():
                self.submit(text)
            return
        if k in ("esc", "ctrl-c") and self.turn_open:
            return self.interrupt()
        if k == "esc":
            if self.input:
                if self.esc_idle_at and time.monotonic() - self.esc_idle_at < 0.3:
                    self.input, self.cur, self.esc_idle_at = "", 0, None
                else:
                    self.esc_idle_at = time.monotonic()
            return
        if k in ("ctrl-c", "ctrl-d"):
            if k == "ctrl-d" and (self.input or self.turn_open):
                return
            if self.armed == k:
                return self.exit("prompt_input_exit")
            self.armed = k
            return
        if k == "shift-tab" and not menu:
            self.agent_mode = MODES[(MODES.index(self.agent_mode) + 1) % len(MODES)]
            return
        if k in ("up", "down") and menu:
            n = len(a["options"]) + 1 if a else len(PERMISSION_OPTIONS)
            menu["sel"] = (menu["sel"] + (1 if k == "down" else -1)) % n
            return
        if k == "newline":
            self.insert("\n")
        elif k == "backspace" and self.cur:
            self.input = self.input[:self.cur - 1] + self.input[self.cur:]
            self.cur -= 1
        elif k == "delete":
            self.input = self.input[:self.cur] + self.input[self.cur + 1:]
        elif k == "left":
            self.cur = max(0, self.cur - 1)
        elif k == "right":
            self.cur = min(len(self.input), self.cur + 1)
        elif k == "home":
            self.cur = self.input.rfind("\n", 0, self.cur) + 1
        elif k == "end":
            nl = self.input.find("\n", self.cur)
            self.cur = len(self.input) if nl < 0 else nl
        elif k == "ctrl-u":
            start = self.input.rfind("\n", 0, self.cur) + 1
            self.input, self.cur = self.input[:start] + self.input[self.cur:], start
        elif k == "ctrl-w":
            m = re.search(r"\S*\s*$", self.input[:self.cur])
            self.input, self.cur = self.input[:m.start()] + self.input[self.cur:], m.start()

    def char(self, ch):
        self.keylog("char " + ch)
        if self.dialog or self.permission:
            return
        if self.asking:
            self.asking["sel"] = len(self.asking["options"])  # typing writes in an answer
        self.insert(ch)

    def csi(self, params, final):
        if final == "Z" or (final == "u" and params == "9;2"):
            return self.key("shift-tab")
        super().csi(params, final)

    # ---- drawing ----
    def render(self, entry, cols):
        kind, text = entry
        lines = text.split("\n")
        if kind == "header":
            return self.header(cols)
        if kind == "you":
            rows = wrap(text, cols - 2)
            return RULE + "─" * min(60, cols) + RESET + "\r\n" + "\r\n".join(
                f"{BLUE}{BOLD}{'> ' if i == 0 else '  '}{r}{RESET}" for i, r in enumerate(rows))
        if kind == "text":
            return "\r\n".join(f"{TEXT}  {line}{RESET}" for line in lines)
        if kind == "tool":
            m = re.match(r"([A-Za-z]+)\((.*)\)$", text)
            if m and m.group(1) == "Bash":
                return f"{AMBER}●{RESET} {AMBER}{BOLD}Ran{RESET} {LIGHT}({m.group(2)}){RESET} {LIGHT}(ctrl+o to expand){RESET}"
            return f"{AMBER}●{RESET} {LIGHT}{text}{RESET}"
        if kind == "out":
            return f"{GREY}⎿  {text}{RESET}"
        if kind == "interrupted":
            return f"{GREY}  ⎿  {text}{RESET}"
        if kind == "err":
            return f"{RED}⚠ {text}{RESET}"
        if kind == "ask":
            return f"{AMBER}{BOLD}?{RESET} " + "\r\n".join(wrap(text, cols - 2))
        if kind == "answer":
            return f"{BLUE}{BOLD}> {text}{RESET}"
        return text

    def header(self, cols):
        right = [f"{BLUE}{BOLD}Antigravity CLI {VERSION}{RESET}", f"{GREY}Example account (Example plan){RESET}",
                 f"{GREY}{self.model} ({self.effort.capitalize()}){RESET}", f"{GREY}{self.folder}{RESET}", ""]
        logo = ["     ▄▀▀▄    ", "    ▀▀▀▀▀▀   ", "   ▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀  ", "  ▄▀▀    ▀▀▄ ", " ▄▀▀ ▀▀▄ ▀▀▄ "]
        return "\r\n".join(f"{BLUE}{l}{RESET} {r}" for l, r in zip(logo, right)) + "\r\n"

    def footer(self, cols, working):
        if self.armed:
            left = f"press {self.armed.replace('-', '+')} again to exit"
        elif self.queue and not self.input:
            left = "  Press up to edit queued messages"
        elif working or self.asking or self.permission or self.dialog:
            left = "esc to cancel" if not self.dialog else ""
        elif self.input:
            left = ""
        else:
            left = "? for shortcuts"
        mode = self.agent_mode
        right = ([(mode, BLUE if mode == "plan" else AMBER), (" · ", GREY)] if mode else []) + [
            (f"{self.model} · {self.effort}", GREY)]
        used = base.cells(left) + sum(base.cells(t) for t, _ in right)
        return [(left, GREY), (" " * max(1, cols - used), "")] + right

    def keys_row(self, parts):
        row = [("  ", "")]
        for i, (k, what) in enumerate(parts):
            row += [(k, BLUE + BOLD), (f" {what}" + (" · " if i < len(parts) - 1 else ""), GREY)]
        return row

    def dynamic(self, rows, cols):
        d = [[]]
        a, p = self.asking, self.permission
        working = self.turn_open and not a and not p
        if self.dialog:
            d += [[("Accessing workspace:", BOLD)]] + [[(r, "")] for r in wrap(self.cwd, cols)]
            d += [[("Do you trust the contents of this project?", BOLD)],
                  [("Antigravity CLI requires permission to read, edit, and execute files here.", "")]]
            d += [[("> " if n == self.dialog["sel"] else "  ", BLUE), (o, BLUE if n == self.dialog["sel"] else "")]
                  for n, o in enumerate(TRUST_OPTIONS)]
            d.append(self.keys_row([("↑/↓", "Navigate"), ("enter", "Confirm")]))
        elif a:
            d += [[("Question", AMBER + BOLD)], [("─" * cols, RULE)], []]
            d += [[(r, BOLD)] for r in wrap(f"Question 1/1: {a['q']}", cols)]
            d.append([])
            for n, opt in enumerate(a["options"] + [self.input or "Write-in..."]):
                sel = n == a["sel"]
                d.append([("> " if sel else "  ", BLUE), (f"{n + 1}. {opt}", BLUE if sel else "")])
            d += [[], self.keys_row([("↑/↓", "Navigate"), ("enter", "Select"), ("esc", "Skip")])]
        elif p:
            word = p["command"].split()[0] if p["command"].split() else p["command"]
            d += [[("Command", AMBER + BOLD)], [("─" * cols, RULE)], [], [("Requesting permission for:", LIGHT + BOLD)],
                  [(f"   {p['command']}", LIGHT)], [], [("Run this command?", BOLD)]]
            for n, opt in enumerate(PERMISSION_OPTIONS):
                sel = n == p["sel"]
                d.append([("> " if sel else "  ", BLUE), (f"{n + 1}. {opt.format(w=word)}", BLUE if sel else "")])
            d += [[], self.keys_row([("↑/↓", "Navigate"), ("tab", "Amend"), ("ctrl+g", "edit/expand command")])]
        else:
            if working:
                d.append([(SPIN[int(time.monotonic() * 10) % len(SPIN)] + "  ", ""), ("Generating...", GREY)])
            for q in self.queue:
                d.append([(f"▸ {' '.join(q.split())} (alt+m to send immediately)", GREY)])
            room = max(1, rows - len(d) - 4)
            if self.input:
                box = self.editor_rows(cols - 2, ">", " ")[-room:]
                box = [[(">" if n == 0 else " ", BLUE if n == 0 else ""), (" ", "")] + r[1:] for n, r in enumerate(box)]
            elif not self.typed and HINTS.get(self.agent_mode):
                # Cut to the box with "..." when too long (captured at 44 and 60 columns).
                hint = HINTS[self.agent_mode]
                hint = hint if len(hint) <= cols - 3 else hint[:max(0, cols - 6)] + "..."
                box = [[(">", BLUE), (" ", ""), (hint, GREY)]]
            else:
                box = [[(">", BLUE)]]
            d += [[("─" * cols, RULE)]] + box + [[("─" * cols, RULE)]]
        d.append(self.footer(cols, working))
        return [base.fit(r, cols)[0] for r in d[-rows:]]

    # ---- lifetime ----
    def start(self):
        self.saved = termios.tcgetattr(0)
        tty.setraw(0)
        self.write("\x1b]7501;?\x07\x1b[?25l\x1b[?2004h\x1b[>4;2m\x1b[>5u")
        r, w = os.pipe()
        os.set_blocking(w, False)
        self.wake_r = r
        signal.set_wakeup_fd(w)
        signal.signal(signal.SIGWINCH, lambda *_: setattr(self, "winch", True))
        for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT):
            signal.signal(sig, lambda n, _: setattr(self, "signal", n))
        if self.sid:
            self.take_lock()
        # Without an answer to the query agy works but never reports.
        self.later(1.0, self.sign_in)
        self.draw()

    def status_ready(self):
        """The terminal answered the query: reports from now on, starting with the sign-in check."""
        self.status_ok = True
        if self.signed_in:
            # A late answer: the state it missed.
            return self.report(*self.reported) if self.reported else None
        self.report("blocked", kind="auth", msg="Sign in required")
        self.later(0.5 if self.resumed else 0.03, self.sign_in)

    def sign_in(self):
        if self.signed_in:
            return
        self.signed_in = True
        if self.dialog:
            # The first prompt's turn runs behind the dialog, unanswered.
            self.report("blocked", kind="permission", msg=TRUST_MSG)
            self.begin()
            return
        self.report("idle")
        self.begin()

    def begin(self):
        if self.begun:
            return
        self.begun = True
        self.gen = self.director()
        self.run_director()
        if self.first_prompt:
            prompt = self.first_prompt
            self.later(1.2, lambda: self.submit(prompt))

    def dialog_key(self, k):
        d = self.dialog
        if k in ("up", "down"):
            d["sel"] = (d["sel"] + 1) % len(TRUST_OPTIONS)
        elif k == "enter" and d["sel"] == 0:
            self.dialog = None
            self.full = True
            self.report("idle")
            self.begin()
        elif k == "enter":
            self.decline()
        elif k == "ctrl-c" and self.armed == "ctrl-c":
            self.exit("other")
        elif k == "ctrl-c":
            self.armed = "ctrl-c"

    def decline(self):
        """"No, exit" on the trust dialog, byte for byte as captured
        (probes/stage5/decline2.bin): no exit screen, no resume line."""
        rows = self.size()[0]
        self.write(f"\x1b[>4m\x1b[<1u\r\x1b[{rows}d\x1b[?1049l\x1b[?25h\x1b[?2004l")
        self.dialog = None
        self.report("idle")
        termios.tcsetattr(0, termios.TCSADRAIN, self.saved)
        sys.exit(0)

    def exit(self, reason, code=0, hung=False):
        self.hung = hung
        if self.dyn_rows:
            self.write("\r" + (f"\x1b[{self.dyn_rows - 1}A" if self.dyn_rows > 1 else "") + "\x1b[J")
            self.dyn_rows = 0
        self.write("\x1b[?25h\x1b[>4m\x1b[<1u\r\n\n\x1b[J\x1b[?2004l\x1b[0 q")
        self.report("idle")
        if self.sid:
            self.write(f"\r\nResume with -c (or command below):\r\nagy --conversation={self.sid}\r\n")
        if hung:
            try:
                termios.tcsetattr(0, termios.TCSADRAIN, self.saved)
            except termios.error:
                pass  # the terminal is gone; nothing to restore
        else:
            termios.tcsetattr(0, termios.TCSADRAIN, self.saved)
        sys.exit(code)


def main():
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if any(a in ("--version", "-v") for a in argv):
        print(VERSION)
        return
    if any(a in ("--help", "-h") for a in argv):
        print(__doc__)
        return
    if not os.isatty(0):
        sys.exit("agy: the stand-in needs a terminal")
    app = Agy(parse_args(argv))
    app.start()
    app.loop()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
